[00:11.76] Ole told me, I'm a fool
[00:16.16] So I walked on down the road a mile
[00:20.28] Went to the house that brings a smile
[00:23.78] Sat upon my grandpa's knee
[00:26.66] And what do you think he said to me?
[00:30.30] (Chorus:)
[00:30.64] When you awake you will remember everything
[00:35.10] You will be hangin' on a string from your...
[00:39.50] When you believe, you will relieve the only soul
[00:44.88] That you were born with to grow old and never know
[00:51.38] Ole showed me the fork in the road
[00:58.16] You can take to the left or go straight to the right,
[01:02.06] Use your days and save your nights
[01:05.10] Be careful where you step, and watch what ya eat,
[01:08.26] Sleep with a light and you got it beat
[01:14.00] (Repeat Chorus)
[01:34.56] Ole warned me, it's a mean old world,
[01:39.84] The street don't greet ya, yes, it's true
[01:43.04] But what am I supposed to do
[01:46.48] Read the writing on the wall
[01:49.30] I heard it when I was very small
[01:52.80] (Repeat Chorus)
[02:14.64] Wash my hands in lye water
[02:17.26] I got a date with the Captain's daughter
[02:21.20] You can go and tell your brother
[02:24.44] We sure gonna love one another all night
[02:33.54] You may be right and you might be wrong
[02:36.34] I ain't gonna worry all day long
[02:46.14] Snow's gonna come and the frost gonna bite
[02:49.42] My old car froze up last night
[02:52.58] Ain't no reason to hang my head
[02:55.78] I could wake up in the mornin' dead
[02:59.16] And if I thought it would do any good
[03:08.36] I'd stand on the rock where Moses stood...
